{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774129305,"nonce":"SArHVEyuHb7bT2el8gGlvROGg7k=","message":"**Per-prompt parameter snapshot needed**\n\nInvestigation of SDKBackend.updateOptions() reveals the parameter staging model:\n- Model: LIVE (applied immediately to current query via setModel())\n- Permission mode: LIVE (applied immediately via setPermissionMode())\n- Max turns: STAGED (next query only)\n- Max cost: STAGED (next query only)\n- Presets/system prompt: STAGED (computed at query start)\n- Allowed tools: HYBRID (permission gate updated immediately, formal list at next query start)\n\n**Gap:** No per-prompt parameter snapshot is stored. buildQueryOptions() constructs options at query start but these are not persisted alongside individual messages. To support viewing per-prompt parameters (via message info/ellipsis action), a new mechanism is needed: snapshot effective options when query starts, associate with the assistant turn, surface in UI details popover.\n\nThis is a sub-task of this issue.","files":null}]}